-- serine. Atoms: 0 carboxyl carbon, 1 and 2 its oxygens, 3 the alpha carbon, 4 its hydrogen, 5 the
-- nitrogen, 6 the beta carbon, 7 and 8 its hydrogens, 9 the beta oxygen, 10 its hydrogen. The beta
-- hydrogens are diastereotopic: their carbon's neighbour is the alpha stereocentre, so no medium
-- identifies them.
num-ser-obs : List Nat
num-ser-obs = cons 4 (cons 7 (cons 8 nil))
